    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "As an example of analysis of a more complex design, consider the nested ANOVA design for mapping QTLs in half-sib families (Chapter 16). In the QTL half-sib design, each sire heterozygous for a marker locus is crossed to n dams and a single offspring is scored from each mating. Evidence of a QTL linked to the marker is indicated if the mean trait values for alternative sire alleles at this marker locus are significantly different. Since a different dam is used for each mating, all offspring from the same sire are half-sibs. The model here is",
      "source_page": 895,
      "printed_page": 875,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_appendix1:p077:b7",
        "Genetics_appendix1:p077:b8"
      ],
